  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254588/assets/54486759fb0aa05eb5348dcc02c3666c1ebfe6458ea56d013ca125acd08fc993.png)\n\nNote that the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ takes any value $y\\le -1$ and any value $y\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{5}{2}$ belongs to the range, $y=-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{4}{5}$ are not in the range. Hence the answer is I only.",
